{:adr-id "2611210000"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-0899 — Other Mining and Quarrying Operations Coordination"
 :date "2026-07-16"
 :author "Cloud Itonami Contributors"
 :status :accepted
 :context
 "ISIC Rev.4 0899 (Other mining and quarrying n.e.c.) had no prior actor
  implementation -- the registry entry pointed at a placeholder repo
  (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-B0899) that was never created. Live registry
  independently re-verified against a fresh clone before proceeding:
  {:id \"0899\" :name \"Other mining and quarrying n.e.c.\" :maturity
  :spec ...} -- confirmed, distinct from already-:implemented siblings
  0892 (peat), 0893 (salt), 0721 (uranium/thorium). Fresh, from-scratch
  scaffold, built as part of a smaller, carefully verified batch after
  an earlier 18-agent haiku batch's 61% defect rate. Module shape
  mirrors sibling cloud-itonami-isic-0893 (Extraction of salt)'s
  verified module shape. ISIC 0899 is a residual (n.e.c.)
  mineral-extraction category (gemstones, quartz, feldspar, abrasives,
  ...); this actor's chosen concrete illustration is quartz/feldspar
  quarrying for industrial abrasives (grinding/blasting media,
  ceramics, glass-batch feedstock)."
 :decision
 {:scope-boundary
  "Coordination-only actor -- a SITE OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor, NOT
   a direct extraction-equipment control authority, NOT an
   environmental-permit-issuing authority. Closed four-op allowlist,
   all :effect :propose: log-extraction-record,
   schedule-extraction-operation, flag-environmental-concern (always
   escalates), coordinate-shipment. An op outside this set is the same
   failure mode as forbidden-scope content, not a separate carve-out."
  :governor-rules
  "Three HARD, permanent, un-overridable checks: (1)
   site-permit-unverified -- target site/permit record must be
   independently :registered?/:verified? in the store, never trusted
   from the proposal's own claim; (2) effect-not-propose -- any :effect
   other than :propose is a claim to directly actuate outside
   governance; (3) scope-exclusion -- any proposal (any op) touching
   extraction-equipment-control (blast-pattern/blast-sequencing/
   drill-pattern/drill-and-blast/excavator-operation/loader-operation/
   crusher-control/conveyor-control/haul-truck-dispatch-control/
   bench-sequencing) or environmental-permit-issuing-authority territory
   (permit issuance/suspension, license suspension, compliance
   enforcement, environmental-permit decision), evaluated
   unconditionally via a lower-cased EN+JA substring scan of the
   proposal's own content. Deliberately does NOT use bare
   'blast'/'発破' as exclusion terms -- only phrase-qualified
   execution/control terms -- because the allowlisted
   schedule-extraction-operation op legitimately describes
   'extraction/blasting scheduling'; a bare-word exclusion would have
   self-blocked every legitimate scheduling proposal (caught live: 6 of
   45 tests failed on the first draft that mirrored the salt actor's
   term list verbatim, fixed by phrase-qualifying the terms).
   Escalation (soft): flag-environmental-concern always, low confidence
   (<0.6). quarryops.phase independently agrees --
   flag-environmental-concern never auto-commits at any phase."
  :module-shape
  "quarryops.store (MemStore, string-keyed site directory seeded with a
   quartz quarry, a feldspar quarry, and an unverified/permit-lapsed
   quartz quarry), advisor (QuarryOpsAdvisor, mock + real-LLM seam via
   langchain.model, plus an :out-of-scope? test hook), governor
   (QuarrySiteGovernor), phase (0->3 rollout), operation (langgraph-clj
   StateGraph), sim (demo driver)."}
 :consequences
